      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just bear in mind that the WGSL backend currently always generates an array member (including *sized* arrays) with a 16-byte stride even if the program only uses SSBOs and contains no uniform binding declaration. These are then always passed as a user-defined function argument following an element-wise copy (see https://paste.googleplex.com/6583555852337152).\n\nWe should keep the potential runtime cost of this in mind when declaring paint or RenderStep uniforms as arrays and probably consider alternatives.\n\nAlso I\u0027m not sure if `UniformManager`\u0027s layout logic currently agrees with the SkSL WGSL backend: I think it assumes that array elements always use a packed layout in std430 mode (see https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/gpu/graphite/UniformManager.cpp;l\u003d131?q\u003dUniformManager.h\u0026ss\u003dchromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc:third_party%2Fskia%2F). So the data for arrays in a SSBO block may not get laid out as expected when using std430.",
      "revId": "4db67054ca80a686c9084c49c84af8212e6e8234",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8780efff_a924b684",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
